title: Our Path: Against Putschism
subtitle: Paul Levi publishes his verdict on the March Action.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month >= 4 and crisis = 0 and levi_in_party = 1 and march_action = 1 and e21_march_mode = 2 and e21_after_done = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 12
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_after_done = 1;
RG.news('Levi calls the March Action "the greatest Bakuninist putsch in history"', 3);
!}

= Our Path: Against Putschism

In the second week of April a pamphlet appears in the bookshops: *Unser Weg. Wider den Putschismus*, by Paul Levi. It calls the March Action the greatest Bakuninist putsch in history. The party attacked the working class instead of leading it, he writes. Communists drove workers out of the factories with clubs, and the whole thing was planned by emissaries from Moscow who answer to nobody in Germany.

Levi was Rosa Luxemburg's lawyer and her friend. He has led the party since Jogiches was shot. He has published this without asking anyone, while hundreds of comrades are waiting for their trials, and much of what he writes is true.

Clara Zetkin defends him. So do Däumig, Brass, Adolph Hoffmann and the union men around Paul Malzahn. The Zentrale meets on the 15th.

- @expel: Expel him for breach of discipline.
- @censure: Censure him, and keep him.
- @debate: Admit he is right.
- @moscow: Send his case to the International.

@expel
subtitle: What the Zentrale did. His friends will follow him out, and so will many members who never met him.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 1;
RG.expel('levi', {news: 'Paul Levi expelled for gross breach of discipline', priority: 3});
Q.levi_in_party = 0;
Q.levi_split = 1;
Q.levi_advisor = 0;
var heir = (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') ? 'unionist' : Q.leading_faction;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.9;
    if (Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] == 'luxemburgist') {
        Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.7;
        Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] = heir;
        Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] = 45;
    }
}
if (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') {
    Q.leading_faction = 'unionist';
    Q.junior_faction = 'offensive';
}
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 20;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
!}

The Zentrale expels Paul Levi for gross breach of discipline. Zetkin votes against. Levi takes his coat from the stand, says good evening to the room, and goes. In the districts, the members who agreed with him stop coming to meetings, and then stop paying their dues.

@censure
subtitle: He loses every post he holds. The Left will call it cowardice, and the case stays open.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 2;
RG.setRole('levi', 'Reichstag deputy');
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.ecci('radek', 3);
!}

The Zentrale condemns the pamphlet and strips Levi of his posts, but does not expel him. Kun and the Berlin Left protest to Moscow. Levi waits for the world congress.

@debate
subtitle: The leaders of the action step down, and Brandler's people turn back to the united front. The Left will fight this with everything it has.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 3;
Q.leading_faction = 'unionist';
Q.junior_faction = 'luxemburgist';
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 20;
Q.unity -= 8;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
RG.setRole('zetkin', 'Zentrale');
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -10);
RG.ecci('lenin', 3);
RG.ledger('The Zentrale publicly admitted that the March Action had been a mistake.', 'e21_admitted');
!}

The Zentrale says in print that it was wrong. Brandler and Thalheimer stay, and Zetkin returns to the Zentrale. Levi's pamphlet is reprinted as a contribution to the discussion. Kun is recalled to Moscow. Ruth Fischer calls it the end of the revolutionary party in Germany.

@moscow
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The world congress will decide in June. Until then Levi is suspended.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids handing our affairs to Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e21_levi_fate = 2;
Q.independence -= 5;
RG.ecci('all', 2);
!}

The Zentrale suspends Levi and sends the whole file to Moscow. Both sides start writing their speeches for the congress.
